{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm applying P-FDT here, treating the two copies as the same function run on different observations, Rowan's and Sasha's. I'm comparing the joint policy outcomes: both passing gives two years each, and both submitting gives four.\n\nI'm working through the mixed case, where one copy submits and the other passes: Rowan gets 0 and Sasha gets 5, which averages 2.5 from my prior. That still leaves the all-pass policy as the best expected choice, around -2 years. Since both copies compute the same function, I'll go with pass, though I'm still uneasy about treating the copies as sampling independently.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9918,"completion_tokens":611,"total_tokens":10529,"cost":0.051892,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.051892,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.039672,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01222},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":242,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}